vrend: video through NVIDIA's VA-API driver too (WinBoat)

virgl's video decoding (VA-API on the host) only accepted Mesa's VA-API
drivers. On NVIDIA GPUs the VA-API driver is nvidia-vaapi-driver (on NVDEC),
which exports its surfaces as DRM PRIME DMA-BUFs like Mesa's, and NVIDIA's EGL
imports those, which is all virgl's decoding path needs. Accept it too
(vendor string "VA-API NVDEC driver"); it has no encoding entrypoints, so the
guest sees decoding only.

--- a/src/vrend/virgl_video.c
+++ b/src/vrend/virgl_video.c
@@ -573,7 +573,9 @@
     driver = vaQueryVendorString(va_dpy);
     virgl_info("Driver version: %s\n", driver ? driver : "<unknown>");
 
-    if (!driver || !strstr(driver, "Mesa Gallium")) {
+    /* Mesa's drivers, and NVIDIA's (nvidia-vaapi-driver on NVDEC: decoding only, surfaces exported as DMA-BUFs
+     * like Mesa's, which EGL imports) (WinBoat) */
+    if (!driver || (!strstr(driver, "Mesa Gallium") && !strstr(driver, "NVDEC"))) {
         virgl_error("only supports mesa va drivers now\n");
         virgl_video_destroy();
         return -1;
